  year        = {2025},
  month       = {Dec},
  note        = {Poster},
  abstract    = {The Kansas Fish Ontology (KFO) is a structured knowledge framework that integrates ecological, taxonomic, and environmental data about fish species across Kansas to support conservation and management. KFO is developed using the Knowledge Acquisition and Representation Methodology (KNARM) and it systematically captures expert knowledge and domain terminology related to species traits, habitats, and environmental dependencies. The ontology was instantiated in GraphDB, and the Fish Ontology Visualizer, a web interface built with Vue.js, Flask and GraphDB, provides interactive exploration of fish-habitat relationships and conservation insights.},
